From: jetson-nixos contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: leave Tegra DRM to the external driver

Nix's config generator reaches TEGRA_HOST1X before DRM_TEGRA. Starting
with DRM_TEGRA=m prevents it from disabling host1x's reverse dependency.
Remove the initial selection; the final config asserts both drivers are off.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -927,7 +927,7 @@
 CONFIG_DRM_SUN8I_DW_HDMI=m
 CONFIG_DRM_SUN8I_MIXER=m
 CONFIG_DRM_MSM=m
-CONFIG_DRM_TEGRA=m
+# CONFIG_DRM_TEGRA is not set
 CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_BOE_TV101WUM_NL6=m
 CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_LVDS=m
 CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_SIMPLE=m
